                        "entry_id": "0186d60b-294f-36a6-a9f5-bf8f43e4f003",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A miniature hard disk."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c3ef1f7-639a-435c-bdff-29bc261dbe5c",
                                "sense_id": "0303301c-8f92-379e-b3a1-5c02604cf8e7",
                                "text": "One-inch disks typically held about 8 to 10 GB and microdrives were either 2 or 4 GB."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2234c24b-d287-3434-b7ac-212fa41b9b60",
                        "entry_id": "0186d60b-294f-36a6-a9f5-bf8f43e4f003",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An early computer storage system using cartridges of looped tape."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90d0981c-7293-411b-a9c9-103b8fd0bdb4",
                                "sense_id": "2234c24b-d287-3434-b7ac-212fa41b9b60",
                                "text": "1984, Alison Maguire, interviewed in SINCLAIR talks... (in Crash magazine, issue 3, April 1984) http://www.crashonline.org.uk/03/sinclair.htm\nThere are lots of things that will benefit from being on a microdrive cartridge but if you release something on microdrive you're only going to sell it to people with microdrive."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb854f6a-3239-4eb5-80f1-b6dd97967ea2",
                                "sense_id": "2234c24b-d287-3434-b7ac-212fa41b9b60",
                                "text": "The Spectrum has its own inexpensive mass storage unit - the microdrive which starts at about £150 for 100k of storage, but this may not be suitable in all cases, since the storage unit may be damaged if turned on with the disc in position."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1073fe54-0d27-4cf0-b871-35f86a9aae94",
                                "sense_id": "2234c24b-d287-3434-b7ac-212fa41b9b60",
                                "text": "Disk interfaces have been around since the year dot, as people soon realised that the microdrive was unreliable, unstable and generally rubbish for the storage of anything, useless except as a rather small beermat."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e0829c9-2978-3fb4-9044-4787e4d99e8d",
                        "entry_id": "0186d60b-294f-36a6-a9f5-bf8f43e4f003",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A device for inserting microelectrodes into the brain."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "069d411e-aa26-4e7b-9ef1-58eab906c42f",
                                "sense_id": "8e0829c9-2978-3fb4-9044-4787e4d99e8d",
                                "text": "The microdrive was invented so that electrodes could be lowered into the brain in order to isolate new neurons."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
